# Append (or merge into) data/conf/postfix/extra.cf on the mailcow host.
#
# Postfix main.cf resolves a repeated parameter by taking the LAST
# definition it parses, and mailcow appends extra.cf to the end of the
# generated main.cf. That means we can override smtpd_recipient_restrictions
# here WITHOUT editing mailcow's generated main.cf directly (which gets
# regenerated and would silently drop manual edits).
#
# Steps:
#   1. Get mailcow's current value so nothing else breaks:
#        docker compose exec postfix-mailcow postconf smtpd_recipient_restrictions
#   2. Copy that value below, and insert our check_recipient_access clause
#      as the FIRST restriction (so unsubscribed recipients are rejected
#      before any other rule has a chance to permit/discard them).
#
# Example (adjust to match what step 1 actually returned for your install):

smtpd_recipient_restrictions =
    check_recipient_access mysql:/opt/postfix/conf/sql/mysql-virtual-unsub-recipient.cf,
    permit_mynetworks,
    permit_sasl_authenticated,
    reject_unauth_destination,
    check_policy_service unix:private/policyd-spf,
    check_policy_service inet:127.0.0.1:10023
